@module flutter-m05 | Navigation
@summary Move between screens with Navigator, named routes and go_router.

@lesson flutter-m05-l01 | Navigation basics | 8
## Learning objectives
- Push and pop screens with Navigator

## Navigation basics
Flutter keeps screens (routes) in a stack. `Navigator.push` adds a route on top; `Navigator.pop` removes it and returns to the previous screen. `MaterialPageRoute` provides platform-appropriate transitions.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void openDetails(BuildContext context) {
  Navigator.of(context).push(
    MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => const Scaffold(body: Center(child: Text('Details')))),
  );
}
```

## Summary
- push adds a screen, pop removes it.
- Routes form a stack.

@lesson flutter-m05-l02 | Named routes | 8
## Learning objectives
- Declare routes by name in MaterialApp

## Named routes
Named routes map strings to builders in `MaterialApp.routes`. Navigate with `Navigator.pushNamed(context, '/settings')`. They are simple but limited for deep links and arguments; most larger apps prefer go_router.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget app() => MaterialApp(
      initialRoute: '/',
      routes: {
        '/': (_) => const Scaffold(body: Center(child: Text('Home'))),
        '/settings': (_) => const Scaffold(body: Center(child: Text('Settings'))),
      },
    );
```

## Summary
- routes maps names to builders.
- Use pushNamed to navigate.

@lesson flutter-m05-l03 | Navigator in depth | 8
## Learning objectives
- Use pushReplacement, pushAndRemoveUntil and maybePop

## Navigator in depth
Beyond push/pop: `pushReplacement` swaps the current screen (e.g. after login), `pushAndRemoveUntil` clears the stack (e.g. logout), and `maybePop` pops only if possible. `PopScope` lets you intercept back navigation, for example to confirm leaving a form.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void afterLogin(BuildContext context) {
  Navigator.of(context).pushAndRemoveUntil(
    MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => const Scaffold(body: Text('Home'))),
    (route) => false,
  );
}
```

## Summary
- Replace screens after login/onboarding.
- PopScope guards back navigation.

@lesson flutter-m05-l04 | Navigation stacks | 8
## Learning objectives
- Reason about the back stack

## Navigation stacks
Every push grows the stack; users expect Back to retrace their steps. Avoid pushing the same screen repeatedly, and clear the stack when entering a new flow (after onboarding or sign-out). Dialogs and bottom sheets are routes too, so `Navigator.pop` closes them.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

bool canGoBack(BuildContext context) => Navigator.of(context).canPop();
```

## Summary
- Dialogs are routes on the same stack.
- Clear the stack when a flow ends.

@lesson flutter-m05-l05 | go_router | 8
## Learning objectives
- Configure declarative routing with go_router

## go_router
`go_router` is the Flutter team's recommended routing package. Routes are URL paths, which makes deep links and web URLs work naturally. Use `MaterialApp.router` with a `GoRouter` and navigate with `context.go('/path')` or `context.push('/path')`.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';

final router = GoRouter(routes: [
  GoRoute(path: '/', builder: (_, __) => const Scaffold(body: Text('Home'))),
  GoRoute(path: '/lesson/:id', builder: (_, state) => Scaffold(body: Text('Lesson ${state.pathParameters['id']}'))),
]);

Widget app() => MaterialApp.router(routerConfig: router);
```

## Summary
- go_router uses URL paths.
- context.go replaces, context.push stacks.

@lesson flutter-m05-l06 | Deep linking | 8
## Learning objectives
- Open specific screens from links

## Deep linking
Deep links open a screen from a URL, e.g. `https://bimo.app/lesson/42`. With go_router, the path is matched automatically. On Android you declare intent filters (App Links) in AndroidManifest.xml; on iOS, Associated Domains (Universal Links).

```dart
// AndroidManifest.xml intent filter (inside <activity>):
// <intent-filter android:autoVerify="true">
//   <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
//   <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
//   <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />
//   <data android:scheme="https" android:host="bimo.app" />
// </intent-filter>
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Paths map links to screens.
- Configure App Links / Universal Links natively.

@lesson flutter-m05-l07 | Nested navigation | 8
## Learning objectives
- Keep separate stacks per tab

## Nested navigation
Apps with bottom tabs often keep a separate navigation stack per tab so switching tabs preserves each tab's history. go_router's `StatefulShellRoute.indexedStack` implements this pattern.

```dart
import 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

final router = GoRouter(routes: [
  StatefulShellRoute.indexedStack(
    builder: (context, state, shell) => Scaffold(body: shell),
    branches: [
      StatefulShellBranch(routes: [GoRoute(path: '/home', builder: (_, __) => const Text('Home'))]),
      StatefulShellBranch(routes: [GoRoute(path: '/profile', builder: (_, __) => const Text('Profile'))]),
    ],
  ),
], initialLocation: '/home');
```

## Summary
- Each tab keeps its own stack.
- Use StatefulShellRoute in go_router.

@lesson flutter-m05-l08 | Route guards | 8
## Learning objectives
- Redirect unauthenticated users

## Route guards
A guard decides whether a route may be shown. go_router's `redirect` callback returns a new location (or null to continue), e.g. send signed-out users to /login. Pass `refreshListenable` so redirects re-run when auth state changes.

```dart
import 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';

bool signedIn = false;

final router = GoRouter(
  redirect: (context, state) => !signedIn && state.matchedLocation != '/login' ? '/login' : null,
  routes: [],
);
```

## Summary
- redirect returns a new path or null.
- Re-evaluate on auth changes.

@lesson flutter-m05-l09 | Passing arguments | 8
## Learning objectives
- Send data to and from screens

## Passing arguments
Pass data forward through constructor parameters (or path/query parameters with go_router). Return data by popping with a value and awaiting the push.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Future<void> pickColor(BuildContext context) async {
  final color = await Navigator.of(context).push<Color>(
    MaterialPageRoute(builder: (ctx) => Scaffold(
      body: Center(child: FilledButton(onPressed: () => Navigator.pop(ctx, Colors.teal), child: const Text('Teal'))),
    )),
  );
  debugPrint('Picked $color');
}
```

## Summary
- Pass data via constructors or URL parameters.
- Await push to receive a result.
